# No empty boxes in hairline grids

`gap-px` + `bg-border` CSS grids paint every track, including leftover ones. Five items in three columns leaves a dead grey box. That cannot ship, on any surface, new or old.

## Do this

- Filled toggles: `Segmented` with `columns`. It snaps via `filledGridColumns`.
- Chip / preset rows: `HairlineGrid`.
- Number tiles: `Scoreboard` / `Score` (`filledCardColumns`).
- Column count must divide the child count at every breakpoint.

```
BAD:  <div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-px bg-border"> with 5 buttons
GOOD: <Segmented columns={3} options={fiveItems} />  // snaps to 5
GOOD: <HairlineGrid preferred={3}>{items}</HairlineGrid>
```

## Do not

- Hand-roll `grid-cols-N` on a `gap-px` / `bg-border` grid.
- Pad with a dummy cell, a spacer `div`, or an empty button.
- Use `auto-fill` on this pattern. Empty tracks still paint.
